IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il41-nouns`
IMPORT `il41-opinions`
IMPORT `il41-representation`
IMPORT `il41-general`

-- THE SEAT LAYER, row IL-41.  The seat is the individual who is a party to, or faces, a court proceeding in which the State takes a side, or whose matter an official decides.  "I" is that person.
-- The Law puts its duties on officials (the Attorney General, the Government, ministers, courts); each question is asked as what the text means for the person: who will present the State's position
-- against me, may the Attorney General appear, can the Government direct the Attorney General in my criminal case.  A judgment the text leaves to someone else is answered NOTHING, never guessed.
-- Each question takes plain inputs and calls the rules in the modules above; no rule is restated here.  The second layer, the recipient of an opinion, is in `il41-seat-recipient.l4`.

§ `Questions of the individual`

§§ `Chapter B: the State's position in my proceeding`

@export Who will present the State's position in my proceeding?
GIVEN `it is a proceeding in the criminal-law domain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding in the criminal-law domain (for example a prosecution of you)?
      `it concerns a power an enactment conferred on the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it concern a power that a law gives the Attorney General himself?
      `it is the representation of a body exercising judicial or quasi-judicial power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the State's side a body that exercises judicial or quasi-judicial power?
      `the Attorney General has given notice under s 8` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Attorney General given notice that the position the Government fixed cannot be presented?
      `the minister concerned considers the position is not or will not be properly presented through the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the minister concerned consider that the position is not, or will not be, properly presented through the Attorney General?
      `the Government has decided that another lawyer presents the position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Government decided that another lawyer will present the position?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Who presents the position of the executive authority`
DECIDE `Who will present the State's position in my proceeding` IS
    `who presents the position of the executive authority` `it is a proceeding in the criminal-law domain` `it concerns a power an enactment conferred on the Attorney General` `it is the representation of a body exercising judicial or quasi-judicial power` `the Attorney General has given notice under s 8` `the minister concerned considers the position is not or will not be properly presented through the Attorney General` `the Government has decided that another lawyer presents the position`

@export Who fixes the position the State takes in my proceeding?
GIVEN `the Government has determined a position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Government determined a position for this proceeding?
GIVETH A `Who fixes the position of the executive authority`
DECIDE `Who fixes the position the State takes in my proceeding` IS
    `who fixes the position of the executive authority` `the Government has determined a position`

@export May the Attorney General appear in my proceeding (s 10(a))?
GIVEN `another lawyer has been chosen under s 9` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has another lawyer been chosen to present the State's position?
      `the proceeding is in a matter touching the criminal-law domain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding in a matter touching the criminal-law domain?
      approval IS A `A way the Attorney General's appearance may be approved` @desc Has the Attorney General's appearance been approved, and by whom?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Attorney General appear in my proceeding` IS
    `s 10(a) lets the Attorney General appear` `another lawyer has been chosen under s 9` `the proceeding is in a matter touching the criminal-law domain` approval

@export May the Attorney General represent this State body in my proceeding (s 11)?
GIVEN kind IS A `A kind of body` @desc Which kind of body is it?
      `the Attorney General consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Attorney General consent?
      `the body consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the body consent?
      `the Knesset's legal adviser consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Knesset's legal adviser consent? (Only the Knesset needs this.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Attorney General represent this State body in my proceeding` IS
    `s 11 lets the Attorney General represent the body` kind `the Attorney General consents` `the body consents` `the Knesset's legal adviser consents`

@export If my case puts the validity of a law in question, must the court tell the Attorney General (s 13)?
GIVEN kind IS A `A kind of body` @desc Which kind of body is deciding?
      `the court saw that it must decide the validity of a law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it see that it must decide whether a law is valid?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `If my case puts the validity of a law in question must the court tell the Attorney General` IS
    `s 13 requires the court to inform the Attorney General` kind `the court saw that it must decide the validity of a law`

§§ `Sections 14 and 15: my criminal case`

@export Can this body direct the Attorney General how to act in my criminal case (s 15(d))?
GIVEN kind IS A `A kind of body` @desc Which kind of body would give the direction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can this body direct the Attorney General how to act in my criminal case` IS
    `s 15(d) lets the body direct the Attorney General how to act in a particular criminal proceeding` kind

§§ `Sections 18 to 20: when does the Law apply to me?`

@export Is the Law in force on this day?
GIVEN day IS A DATE @desc Which day?
      commencement IS A DATE @desc On which day does the Law commence? (Section 18 gives 1 January 2027.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Law in force on this day` IS
    `the Law is in force on` day commencement
